commit f9d81b31
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 11:56:24 -0600
subject: feat(observability): add AI Error Analyst — analyze captured failures with your own models

- New POST /api/analyze-error: loads a requestDetail by id, builds a compact
  diagnostic context (provider, model, status, error, request, provider
  response — all truncated), and runs it through the normal internal pipeline
  (getModelInfo → getProviderCredentials → handleChatCore) using
  settings.analyzeErrorModel (default oc/mimo-v2.5-free). Any connected
  provider works — no new auth surface.
- RequestDetailsTab drawer: 'Analyze error with AI' button on failed requests,
  shows the model used, loading state, error state, and the analysis result.
- settingsRepo: analyzeErrorModel default added.

Tests: tests/unit/analyze-error.test.js — 4 tests (400 missing id, 404 not
found, 400 no credentials without calling chatCore, 200 with analysis text +
context assertions). All pass.

Part of: Observability & Conversation Analytics plan (Phase P2)


